1. Definitions

"Backstory Group", "we", "us" and "our" mean Backstory Group Limited.

"EWAI" means the Engineering With AI software, including its source code,
runtime, command-line tools, dashboard, documentation, templates and other
materials distributed with it.

"Official Package" means an unmodified release of EWAI published by Backstory
Group through npm or another channel that we identify as official.

"Project Content" means the source code, specifications, documentation,
configuration, records and other material that you or your organisation create,
provide or maintain in a project that uses EWAI.

"Output" means material produced through the ordinary intended use of the
Official Package, including generated or materialised project source code,
specifications, plans, reports, documentation and other project artefacts.
Output does not include EWAI itself or a Modified Version.

"Extension" means independently written software that interoperates with EWAI
through a documented or ordinarily supported interface without copying,
modifying or incorporating any part of EWAI.

"Modified Version" means EWAI, or any part of it, that has been modified,
adapted, translated, rearranged, combined into another product, or used to
create a derivative work.

"you" means the individual or legal entity accepting this licence. People who
work for you may use the Official Package on your behalf, provided that you
ensure they comply with this licence.

2. Permission to use the Official Package

Subject to this licence, Backstory Group gives you a non-exclusive, worldwide,
