4. Independent Extensions and integrations

You may create, use, license, distribute and commercialise Extensions.
Interoperating with EWAI through a documented or ordinarily supported interface
does not, by itself, make an Extension a Modified Version.

An Extension must not:

- copy, incorporate, modify or redistribute EWAI source code;
- bypass technical restrictions or licence controls;
- imply that it is made, approved or endorsed by Backstory Group without our
  written permission; or
- use Backstory Group trade marks except to describe truthful compatibility.

5. Source transparency

Where Backstory Group makes EWAI source code available, you may view and inspect
it for transparency, evaluation, security review, compliance review and
understanding how the Official Package works. You may make the copies that are
technically necessary for those purposes, including a local inspection copy.

Access to the source code does not give you permission to use it to create a
Modified Version, to maintain an unofficial distribution, or to exercise any
right not expressly granted by this licence. Any technical ability supplied by
